sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User (Clinician / Patient / Staff)
    participant Client as Frontend SPA
    participant Server as Backend API
    participant Mail as Email Dispatcher
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas

    User->>Client: Enters Email / NIC and Password
    Client->>Server: POST /api/auth/login
    Server->>DB: Query User by identifier
    alt Password Mismatch / Account Locked
        Server-->>Client: HTTP 401 "Invalid Credentials" (Rate limited)
    else Password Verified
        Server->>Server: Generate cryptographically secure 6-digit OTP
        Server->>DB: Insert OTPSession (expires: 300 seconds TTL)
        Server->>Mail: Dispatch OTP to registered email
        Server-->>Client: HTTP 200 { requireOtp: true, sessionId: "..." }
    end

    User->>Client: Enters received 6-digit OTP code
    Client->>Server: POST /api/auth/verify-otp { sessionId, code }
    Server->>DB: Lookup OTPSession by sessionId
    alt OTP Expired or Code Mismatch
        Server-->>Client: HTTP 400 "Invalid or Expired OTP"
    else OTP Valid
        Server->>DB: Delete OTPSession (Single-use consumption)
        Server->>Server: Sign Access JWT (Role, User ID, Expiry)
        Server->>Server: Generate Refresh Session Token
        Server-->>Client: HTTP 200 { token, user: { role, preferredLanguage } }
        Client->>Client: Store JWT in secure memory / session state
        Client-->>User: Redirect to role-specific dashboard
    end
